  "response_text": "Avoiding opportunities due to fear of failure can be a common challenge, but tracking measurable progress can help you stay motivated and make progress towards your goals. Here are some warning signs to watch for:\n\n  1. You're avoiding opportunities because you're afraid of failure, but you're not sure what failure looks like or how to measure it.\n  2. You're avoiding opportunities because you're afraid of the unknown, but you're not sure what the unknown is or how to prepare for it.\n  3. You're avoiding opportunities because you're afraid of the consequences of failure, but you're not sure what the consequences are or how to mitigate them.\n  4. You're avoiding opportunities because you're afraid of the risk of failure, but you're not sure what the risk is or how to manage it.\n  5. You're avoiding opportunities because you're afraid of the uncertainty of failure, but you're not sure what the uncertainty is or how to navigate it.\n\nTo overcome these warning signs, it's important to take a proactive approach and take steps to measure your progress towards your goals. This can help you stay motivated and make progress towards your objectives, even in the face of fear of failure.",
